unction CO","description":"ESFGJT\n\nA strong low pressure system off the Pacific Coast will begin to draw\nin tropical moisture associated with Topical Storm Rachel this\nweekend. This strong southerly fetch will draw anomalously high\nmoisture content across the Desert Southwest and into eastern Utah\nand western Colorado. The chance for widespread precipitation\nincreases Saturday evening into Sunday. Total precipitation forecasts\nrange from 1 to 3 inches across high terrain, with highest amounts\nfavoring the Uintas, Tavaputs and the Southwest San Juan mountains.\n\nEmbedded thunderstorms are also possible Sunday afternoon, increasing\nthe threat for flash flooding across vulnerable terrain. While\nconfidence in location and rainfall rates remain low at this time,\nthe potential for rapidly rising rivers, streams, normally dry\narroyos and slot canyons are possible Sunday through Monday.\n\nPlease follow the evolving forecast, especially if your plans\nincluding recreating or commuting across eastern Utah and western\nColorado Sunday onward. Also, keep in mind weather potential above\nyour location and upstream, particularly for those who reside below\nsensitive terrain like recent burn scars.","ends":"2026-10-12T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Delta, CO; Dolores, CO; Garfield, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Mesa, CO; Moffat, CO; Montezuma, CO; Montrose, CO; Ouray, CO; Rio Blanco, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Daggett, UT; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT; Uintah, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-11T18:07:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 111807 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1207 PM MDT Sun Oct 11 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - An additional 1-2\" of rain is expected over the high terrain through Monday, with locally higher amounts likely over the Uintas. Flooding/flash flooding remains possible, but not probable. - A Wind Advisory is in effect through 6 AM Monday with valley win","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-11T18:53:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Gusty winds up to 40-50 mph continue through the overnight hours, with showers and storms decreasing in intensity this evening. Wet weather remains in the forecast through at least mid week, with snow chances increasing over the higher terrain as the week progresses. Critical fire weather conditions are not anticipated, but watch out for windy conditions over the next handful of days","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":null,"aviation":{"icao":"KHDN","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KHDN 111956Z AUTO 24016G21KT 10SM SCT085 24/04 A2982 RMK AO2 PK WND 23029/1923 SLP019 T02390044","temp_f":75,"wind_dir":240,"wind_kt":16,"gust_kt":21,"visibility":"10+","cover":"SCT","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1009.9,"observed":1791748560,"raw_taf":"TAF KHDN 111740Z 1118/1218 11017KT P6SM VCSH SCT040 OVC060 FM111900 22014G25KT P6SM VCSH SCT040 BKN060 TEMPO 1120/1124 VRB20G35KT 4SM -TSRA BKN060CB FM120000 18011G24KT P6SM SCT060 BKN080 PROB30 1200/1206 4SM -SHRA BKN060 FM120600 20013G20KT P6SM SCT060 BKN090 WS020/21040KT FM121200 15008KT P6SM SCT060 BKN080","url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KHDN&hours=0"},"airgradient":null,"airnow":null,"openmeteo_aq":{"pm25":2.3,"pm10":3.5,"co":107,"no2":0.3,"so2":0.2,"o3":80,"european_aqi":30,"us_aqi":35,"time":"2026-10-11T14:00"},"usgs":null,"snotel":null,"cdot_camera":{"id":"969","name":"US 40 MP 040.35 WB at Elk Spings Ranch","lat":40.37032,"lon":-108.389,"distance_km":48.7,"imageUrl":null,"pageUrl":"https://maps.cotrip.org/?lat=40.37032&lon=-108.389&zoom=12"},"cdot_rwis":null,"cdot_road